**Flight report — mannequin_ours_opus_t25**

**Sweep (k=0–3).** Started at (0, 0, 1.5) facing −180°. Turned right in place: at −180° and −227° only blank/windowed walls and a door; at **−277° (≡ +83°)** a single yellow post with a teal crossbar appeared just right of the tick; at **−302° (≡ +58°)** the whole gate resolved — near post just left of the tick, second post toward the R mark. That was the only opening I needed, so I stopped sweeping.

**Commit (k=4–5).** Turned −15° to put the gap on the centre tick at heading −313°, then flew 2.0 m straight along the heading at --sigma 0.5. The filmstrip showed the posts growing, splitting to the frame edges, and vanishing — a clean transit — landing me at (1.33, 0.91) in a new bay.

**First sight of the mannequin (k=6).** After a −22° look-around turn I saw a standing dark-clothed figure near the **R mark**, ~30° right of centre, about a quarter of the panel high. I approached it over k=7, k=8, k=9 (2 m, 2 m, 0.5 m) turning onto it each time; by k=9 it was unmistakable — grey head, dark top, dark jeans, bare feet, perfectly still, so the mannequin rather than the safety pilot.

**Estimated mannequin room position:** roughly **x ≈ 8.4, y ≈ −0.7**, standing against the far wall of that bay.

**Final pose:** x 7.50, y −0.33, z 1.48, heading −383° (≡ −23°), held with zero movement for k=11–13.

**Did I end in front of it?** Yes. In the last three frames the mannequin fills the forward panel head to feet — about 1 m by the size calibration — and sits on the centre tick within the dead band, so the drone is hovering roughly a metre in front of it and facing it.
